[Applause]  [Music]  welcome to februari it's a month of love  so we've got plenty of historical  violence retro gameplay and trippy  puzzles to solve alright maybe it's not  so romantic after all but in any case  let's talk about the biggest games  launching soon and don't forget to  subscribe to catch all the hottest  releases every week neyo started  development in 2004 but now we're  finally getting our hands on the brutal  samurai combat game if you like dark  souls you'll feel right at home neo puts  you in control of real life Western  samurai William Adams who's tasked with  hunting down yokai across a dark  fictionalized version of San Goku era  Japan you can expect to tangle with a  bunch of frightening mythical creatures  along the way so you have to use a  variety of katanas great axes magic  scrolls and more just to survive neo  comes exclusively to ps4 on Tuesday  februari 7 and if you're not quite sure  about taking on the challenge head over  to gamespot for our review now let's  jump over to steam where there's a  cutesy 3d platformer you might have  missed last week poi takes its cues from  nintendo 64 classics like super mario 64  and banjo kazooie and it stars two young  kids who travel across levels full of  hills and snow fields and deserts to  become master explorers there are over  100 medallions to collect along the way  and you'll have to master all sorts of  tricky jumps and special tools to grab  them all the best part you don't have to  wait toys available on PC right now  let's stick with steam for the rest of  the week because there are a ton of  fresh indie games on the way leading the  charge is splasher this 2d platformer  arms you with a paint cannon and you'll  have to use the many colors of the  rainbow to make it through the ink Corp  factory watery blue ink works like a  jetpack red ink lets you stick to walls  and yellow ink lets you bounce off of  surfaces like a trampoline if you want  to rescue your fellow splashers from the  evil a duct or you can do it on PC on  the 7th  now we'll spend some time with induction  better yet let's rewind time because  that's what this abstract puzzle game is  all about it focuses on cause and effect  so you'll have to keep track of how  pushing switches moving blocks and  crossing bridges affects your little  moving cube induction may seem simple on  the surface but all those elements can  get totally borked if you alter  something in the past without thinking  it's colorful its angular and you can  start solving its 50-plus puzzles on PC  on the 7th speaking of going back in  time gunmetal Arcadia looks like a game  straight out of the NES era the sequel  to gunmetal Arcadia 0 combines that  retro style with platforming and a good  dose of action with over 75 weapons and  items you'll have to use a combination  of bombs swords scrolls and all sorts of  knickknacks as you help the tech elves  fight against the evil unmade Empire if  you're yearning for a roguelike game  that looks just like you're playing on  an old CRT TV set you can give gunmetal  arcadia look on pc on the 7th and those  are the biggest games will be playing  this week as always remember that  release dates are based on retailer  listings and are subject to change  thanks for watching guys I'll see you  next time  [Music]  you  [Music]

